A Festival Convenes
Made entirely in code. No stock footage, no generated video, no generated images.

TYPEFACE
  Archivo (variable roman, weight 100–900, width 62–125)
  Omnibus-Type · https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/archivo
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 · the licence text ships beside the font in fonts/OFL.txt
  Used for every word in the film.

SOUND
  Score and foley are synthesised in this project (mix.py) with numpy and scipy:
  kick, closed hat, rim, bass, marimba, glockenspiel, vibraphone, sine glide, and the print
  foley (ruling pen, block snap, letterpress clack, guillotine snick, paper slap and slide,
  numeral thunk, rubber stamp, carriage return). No sample libraries, no recordings,
  no third-party audio of any kind.

PICTURE
  Drawn frame by frame with Canvas 2D in this project (film.js), captured headless and
  encoded with ffmpeg. Lemo-Opuscar supplies the render and audio tooling
  (https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, code MIT); none of its demo material,
  artwork or music is in this film.

CONTENT
  Every figure, name and quoted phrase is from the source deck, "A festival convenes. It does not
  produce.", Atlanta Design Festival, prepared for Bernard by Daniel, October 2026, supplied by the
  client. The six institutions are named as set type, not as logos or marks. The film carries no
  third-party trademark, photograph, footage, map or dataset.

  Figures as the deck states them: website traffic down 25% (32,342 sessions in 2025 against 21,308
  so far in 2026); eleven months with no money coming in; 60% of tickets sold in the last week;
  $14,685 tour revenue in 2026; Portland peaked at $239,630 and shut in 2021; 9,400 on the list at
  37% open and 16% click; sponsorship $1,000-$20,000, website advertising $625-$8,500, Industry
  Resources $2,500 each, directory listings $50 a year, the store $42 a shirt; $450 to file the
  nonprofit, around six months to the determination letter.

  The deck says two of the six revenue lines have ever been sold and does not say which two. The
  film shows two of six marks filled rather than naming any line.

